---
// Cookie policy. The storage tables must match what the client modules write:
// theme.ts, consent.ts, utm.ts, ab.ts and the loaders in analytics.ts.
import Legal from '../layouts/Legal.astro';
import { site } from '../data/site';

const toc = [
  { id: 'about', title: 'Cookies and similar storage' },
  { id: 'your-choice', title: 'Your choice' },
  { id: 'what-we-store', title: 'What this site stores' },
  { id: 'clearing', title: 'How to clear storage in your browser' },
  { id: 'changes', title: 'Changes and contact' },
];

interface Item {
  name: string;
  type: string;
  purpose: string;
  life: string;
}

const necessary: Item[] = [
  { name: 'viaclin-theme', type: 'localStorage', purpose: 'Your light or dark choice.', life: 'Until you clear it' },
  {
    name: 'viaclin-consent',
    type: 'localStorage',
    purpose: 'Your cookie choice and the date you made it.',
    life: '6 months, then we ask again',
  },
];

const analytics: Item[] = [
  {
    name: 'viaclin-utm',
    type: 'sessionStorage',
    purpose: 'Campaign values for the visit, such as utm_source and the landing page. They travel with a contact form you send.',
    life: 'Ends with the tab',
  },
  { name: '_ga', type: 'Cookie, Google Analytics', purpose: 'Tells one visitor from another.', life: 'Up to 2 years' },
  {
    name: '_ga_<container>',
    type: 'Cookie, Google Analytics',
    purpose: 'Keeps the state of a session.',
    life: 'Up to 2 years',
  },
];

const insights: Item[] = [
  {
    name: 'viaclin-ab',
    type: 'localStorage',
    purpose: 'The test group you were placed in, so that you see the same version of a page on each visit.',
    life: '90 days',
  },
  {
    name: '_clck',
    type: 'Cookie, Microsoft Clarity',
    purpose: 'Holds the Clarity visitor ID and preferences for this site.',
    life: '1 year',
  },
  {
    name: '_clsk',
    type: 'Cookie, Microsoft Clarity',
    purpose: 'Joins the page views of one visit into a single session recording.',
    life: '1 day',
  },
  {
    name: 'CLID',
    type: 'Cookie, Microsoft domain',
    purpose: 'Marks the first time Clarity saw this browser on any site that uses Clarity.',
    life: 'Set by Microsoft',
  },
  {
    name: 'ANONCHK',
    type: 'Cookie, Microsoft domain',
    purpose: 'Shows whether MUID passes to ANID, an advertising cookie. Clarity does not use ANID, so the value is 0.',
    life: 'Set by Microsoft',
  },
  { name: 'MR', type: 'Cookie, Microsoft domain', purpose: 'Shows whether to refresh MUID.', life: 'Set by Microsoft' },
  {
    name: 'MUID',
    type: 'Cookie, Microsoft domain',
    purpose: 'Identifies a browser that visits Microsoft sites. Microsoft uses it for advertising, site analytics and operations.',
    life: 'Set by Microsoft',
  },
  {
    name: 'SM',
    type: 'Cookie, Microsoft domain',
    purpose: 'Keeps MUID in step across Microsoft domains.',
    life: 'Set by Microsoft',
  },
];

const groups = [
  {
    title: 'Necessary',
    label: 'Necessary storage',
    note: 'On at all times. The site cannot honour your settings without these two items.',
    items: necessary,
  },
  {
    title: 'Analytics, after you accept',
    label: 'Analytics storage',
    note: 'Google Analytics 4 shows us which pages are read and how visitors arrive.',
    items: analytics,
  },
  {
    title: 'Insights, after you accept',
    label: 'Insights storage',
    note: 'Microsoft Clarity heatmaps and session replays, and tests that compare two versions of a page.',
    items: insights,
  },
];
---

<Legal
  title="Cookie policy: Viaclin"
  description="What viaclin.com stores in your browser, why and for how long. Analytics and insights stay off until you accept, and you can change your choice at any time."
  lead="What this site stores in your browser, why, for how long, and how to change your choice."
  path="/cookies"
  toc={toc}
>
  <h2 id="about">Cookies and similar storage</h2>
  <p>
    A cookie is a small text file that a website asks your browser to keep. Browsers also offer two similar stores,
    localStorage and sessionStorage, which hold small values for a site without sending them to the server on every
    request. This site uses all three.
  </p>
  <p>
    In Ireland the ePrivacy Regulations (S.I. No. 336 of 2011) cover each of these, not cookies alone. The rule is
    short: a site may store what it needs to provide the service you asked for, and it needs your consent for anything
    else. Where stored values relate to a person, the GDPR applies as well, and the
    {' '}<a href="/privacy">privacy notice</a> covers that side.
  </p>

  <h2 id="your-choice">Your choice</h2>
  <p>
    When analytics or insight tools are switched on, a banner asks before anything loads. It offers three options of
    equal weight: accept all, reject all, or choose by group. Until you choose, nothing in the analytics or insights
    groups loads. Google Consent Mode runs with every signal set to denied, and it stays that way if you reject. The
    advertising signals stay denied whatever you choose. While no such tool is switched on, there is nothing to ask
    about, so no banner appears.
  </p>
  <p>
    We keep your choice for 6 months and then ask again. You can change it at any time with the button below, or with
    the "Cookie settings" button in the footer of every page.
  </p>
  <p class="no-print">
    <button class="btn btn--secondary" type="button" data-consent-open>Change cookie settings</button>
  </p>
  <p>
    When you withdraw consent, the site stops that tool and deletes what it can reach: the Google Analytics cookies,
    {' '}<code>_clck</code> and <code>_clsk</code>, your test group and the stored campaign values. Cookies on Microsoft
    domains are outside its reach. To remove those, clear them in your browser. The steps are further down this page.
  </p>

  <h2 id="what-we-store">What this site stores</h2>
  <p>The site sorts what it stores into three groups. The names below are the ones your browser will show you.</p>

  {groups.map((group) => (
    <>
      <h3>{group.title}</h3>
      <p>{group.note}</p>
      <div class="table-wrap" tabindex="0" role="region" aria-label={group.label}>
        <table>
          <thead>
            <tr>
              <th scope="col">Name</th>
              <th scope="col">Type</th>
              <th scope="col">What it does</th>
              <th scope="col">How long it lasts</th>
            </tr>
          </thead>
          <tbody>
            {group.items.map((item) => (
              <tr>
                <th scope="row"><code>{item.name}</code></th>
                <td>{item.type}</td>
                <td>{item.purpose}</td>
                <td>{item.life}</td>
              </tr>
            ))}
          </tbody>
        </table>
      </div>
    </>
  ))}

  <p>
    Google and Microsoft set their own cookies once you consent. The Google Analytics cookies, <code>_clck</code> and
    {' '}<code>_clsk</code> sit on this site's domain. The rest sit on Microsoft domains, and Microsoft decides how long
    they last. Both companies publish their own lists:
    {' '}<a href="https://support.google.com/analytics/answer/11397207" rel="noopener noreferrer">Google Analytics cookie usage</a>{' '}
    and <a href="https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/clarity/setup-and-installation/clarity-cookies" rel="noopener noreferrer">Microsoft Clarity cookies</a>.
  </p>

  <h2 id="clearing">How to clear storage in your browser</h2>
  <p>Every browser lets you see and delete what a site has stored. The menu names differ a little.</p>
  <ul>
    <li>
      <strong>Chrome and Edge:</strong> open Settings, go to the privacy section and choose the option to delete
      browsing data. Tick cookies and other site data.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Firefox:</strong> open Settings, go to the privacy and security section, find cookies and site data, and
      choose to clear data.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Safari:</strong> open Settings, go to Privacy and choose to manage website data. On an iPhone or iPad,
      open the Settings app, choose Safari, then clear history and website data.
    </li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    To clear this site alone, open the site information panel beside the address bar and choose the cookies or site
    data option.
  </p>
  <p>
    Clearing storage also removes your cookie choice and your theme. When analytics or insight tools are switched on,
    the banner asks again on your next visit. If you block all site data, the site still works. It cannot remember
    your theme or your cookie choice, so analytics and insights stay off.
  </p>

  <h2 id="changes">Changes and contact</h2>
  <p>
    We update this page when the site starts or stops using a cookie or a storage item. The date at the top shows when
    the text last changed.
  </p>
  <p>Questions about this policy: <a href={`mailto:${site.email}`}>{site.email}</a></p>
</Legal>

<style>
  code {
    font-family: ui-monospace, 'Cascadia Mono', Consolas, monospace;
    font-size: 0.92em;
    color: var(--fg);
    overflow-wrap: anywhere;
  }

  th code,
  thead th {
    white-space: nowrap;
  }

  /* column floors: the table scrolls inside its frame before a column gets too tight to read */
  th:nth-child(2),
  td:nth-child(2) {
    min-width: 8.5rem;
  }

  td:nth-child(3) {
    min-width: 15rem;
  }

  th:nth-child(4),
  td:nth-child(4) {
    min-width: 9rem;
  }

  @media print {
    th,
    td {
      min-width: 0 !important;
    }
  }
</style>
